\viewkind4\uc1\pard\tx3780\tx3960\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. I Want the Spirit of power within, 
\par Of love, and of a healthful mind:
\par Of power, to conquer inbred sin ;
\par Of love, to Thee and all mankind ;
\par Of health, that pain and death defies,
\par Most vigorous when the body dies.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. When shall I hear the inward voice
\par Which only faithful souls can hear?
\par Pardon, and peace, and heavenly joys
\par Attend the promised Comforter:
\par O come! And righteousness divine,
\par And Christ, and all with Christ, are mine.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. O that the Comforter would come!
\par Nor visit as a transient guest,
\par But fix in me His constant home,
\par And take possession of my breast,
\par And fix in me His loved abode,
\par The temple of indwelling God,
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Come, Holy Ghost, my heart inspire!
\par Attest that I am born again;
\par Come, and baptize me now with fire,
\par Nor let Thy former gift be vain:
\par I cannot rest in sins forgiven;
\par Where is the earnest of my heavens?
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Where the indubitable seal
\par That ascertains the kingdom mine?
\par Thou powerful stamp I long to feel,
\par The signature of love divine:
\par O shed it in my heart abroad,
\par Fullness of love, of heaven, of God.\tab 
\par                                            Amen.
\par \i 
\par \pard\i0\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2 
\par }

